{"name":"Olivia","hex":"#996622","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Olivia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Latin.","A city, the county seat of Renville County, Minnesota, United States, named for a female station agent named Olive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Olivia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Olivia (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Olivia is a feminine given name in the English language. It is derived from Latin oliva, olive. Both Oliva and Olivia were Latinate forms in use in English-speaking countries as early as the 13th century. Olive was in common use as a vernacular form. Though not invented by William Shakespeare, the name was popularized by a character in Twelfth Night."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Olivia%2C_from_Twelfth_Night.jpg/330px-Olivia%2C_from_Twelfth_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olivia_(name)","wikidata":"Q632264"},{"title":"Olivia Longott","blocks":[{"text":"Olivia Theresa Longott is an American R&B singer. She is best known for performing with the hip hop group G-Unit and also formerly known as a cast member on the VH1 reality television series Love & Hip Hop: New York."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Olivia_by_David_Alvarado.jpg/330px-Olivia_by_David_Alvarado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olivia_Longott","wikidata":"Q270700"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Olivia_Langdon_Clemens%2C_1869.jpg/500px-Olivia_Langdon_Clemens%2C_1869.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Olivia_Langdon_Clemens%2C_1869.jpg/500px-Olivia_Langdon_Clemens%2C_1869.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig